From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 02:34:24 -0400
Subject: peek: links leaving a pinned tab's site open over the window

A pinned tab behaves like an app (docs/PRODUCT.md, "Peek"): a link click
that would leave its site opens a peek, a page over the window, instead of
navigating the pinned page away. Escape or a click on the scrim dismisses
it; Cmd+O or the button promotes the very same WebContents into a new
active tab. "Pinned" is either tier: Chromium-pinned or pinned in a Space.

PeekNavigationThrottle is registered from Chromium's throttle list for
renderer-initiated main-frame navigations in pinned tabs of normal windows
and cancels the ones ShouldPeek() picks: a user's link click (not a script
redirect, so sign-in bounces still work; not a form post), http(s) on both
sides, to a different eTLD+1. PeekView is a layered child of the browser
view, the same arrangement as the command bar, and owns its WebContents;
promotion hands it to chrome::AddWebContents.

Why: the product's pinned-tab model needs Peek or pinning is a bookmark.
Removable when: never, unless the pinned-tab model changes.
